      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4a48959f-6220-5b46-83ea-945f4cb60c12",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Pomeranian, Sporting Lucas Terrier, Japanese Spitz, Elkhounds\n- Places: Pomerania, Germany, Poland, Central Europe, Fennoscandia\n- Concepts: Spitz-type dogs, terrier type, dog breed standards, hunting\n\nFacts:\n- The Pomeranian, also called the Pom or Pom Pom, is a Spitz-type dog breed named after the Pomerania region in Germany and Poland in Central Europe.\n- The Sporting Lucas Terrier is a small dog breed of the terrier type.\n- Dog breed standards for the Japanese Spitz vary around the world, but the breed is always larger than the smaller Pomeranian.\n- Elkhounds are a group of Fennoscandian dog breeds in the Spitz type that are used for hunting elk or moose and other large animals.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "b0fe8f76-47df-5003-9c83-7604c38661fa",
        "text": "Page: Pomeranian (dog). Sentence: The Pomeranian (often known as a Pom or Pom Pom) is a breed of dog of the Spitz type that is named for the Pomerania region in Germany and Poland in Central Europe.\nPage: Sporting Lucas Terrier. Sentence: The Sporting Lucas Terrier is a small breed of dog of the terrier type.\nPage: Japanese Spitz. Sentence: There are varying standards around the world as to the ideal size of the breed, but they are always larger than their smaller cousins, the Pomeranian.\nPage: Elkhound. Sentence: Elkhounds are a group of Fennoscandian dog breeds belonging to the Spitz-type dogs and used for hunting elk/moose and other large animals.",
